  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Wednesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: The high pressure system to the east \ncontinues to feed monsoonal moisture into eastern Nevada, with \nstorms already ongoing in White Pine and southeastern Elko county.\nThese storms are expected to spread into northeastern Elko county\nthis afternoon before dying out around sunset. Hazardous fire \nbehavior from thunderstorm winds continues to be a threat today, \nas well as new ignitions from lightning. Monsoonal moisture \ncontinues in eastern Nevada through the weekend but beginning \ntomorrow it\u2019s joined by an influx of Pacific moisture from the \nremnants of Tropical Storm Iselle. This additional moisture is \nexpected to result in widespread showers and thunderstorms across \nthe forecast area. Additionally, a level 1 Marginal risk of \nexcessive rainfall is in place for much of the forecast area \ntomorrow and Saturday. Storms may also pose a debris flow threat \nto recent fires and fresh burn scars. Overcast skies and rain\ncooled air will also decrease high temperatures below normal\nvalues. The tropical moisture dissipates by Sunday but some \nmonsoonal moisture will still be capable of spawning isolated \nthunderstorms through midweek as the high pressure center looks to\ntake its time in breaking down.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in thunderstorm\nactivity through Saturday. SST and SerpISC were again used to\nbetter represent thunderstorm probabilities in eastern NV between\n18Z today and 03Z tomorrow.",
